Wiring points:
- cmd/teslasync/main.go already builds outboundAPILogSink (line 239) and asserts it satisfies httputil.APICallSink (line 247). Sink wiring to migrated adapters happens here (Prompt 13).
- cmd/notification-worker/main.go runs in its own process; needs its own asyncAPICallLogger + APICallSinkAdapter to register the notification.SetSink before starting the MQTT consumer. notification.Send is called from the worker (internal/notification/worker.go) and from internal/automation/action/notify.go via the automation worker.
- cmd/automation-worker/main.go runs in its own process; reaches notification.Send via action.NewNotifyExecutor, and constructs tesla.NewClient (which calls auth.tokenRequest indirectly when refreshing tokens). Needs its own asyncAPICallLogger + APICallSinkAdapter wired to notification.SetSink and tesla.SetAuthSink.
- cmd/export-worker/main.go is NOT in allowed files; only export jobs run there (no outbound HTTP through the migrated adapters).
=== REASONING ===
Tesla Fleet API client (internal/tesla/client.go) stays out of the migration: its doRequest()/doRequestWithToken() wrap each call with SetLogCallback so service="tesla-api" rows are written exactly once. Wiring httputil.NewClient + sink there would double-record every call (sink_test.go enforces the single-source rule). The tesla.Client struct is therefore left untouched; auth.tokenRequest is given a separate package-level authHTTPClient with Name="tesla-auth" so OAuth code/refresh exchanges land in api_call_logs distinctly from Fleet API rows.

internal/tesla/client_auth.go::GetPartnerToken still uses Client.httpClient (Fleet API client). That is pre-existing behaviour: today GetPartnerToken is unlogged because it bypasses doRequest's SetLogCallback path. client_auth.go is NOT in the allowed-files list for this prompt, and the prompt's gate does not enforce it; partner-token migration is out of scope.

internal/adapter/tesla/client.go is the alternative hexagonal Tesla adapter. grep shows it has zero importers anywhere in cmd/ or internal/ — only its own mapper.go uses the same package. It is not wired into production paths. Per the prompt instruction, it is left as-is and this decision is documented here.

Pattern across packages: each migrated package owns a package-level *http.Client constructed via httputil.NewClient at init with no Sink (preserves today's behaviour for tests/consumers that never call SetSink). main.go (and each worker main) installs the sink via Set* setter; the setter rebuilds the client with the Sink wired in. RWMutex protects the swap so request goroutines reading the client pointer never race the setter. This mirrors the existing api.SetAPICallLogger pattern in api_call_log_middleware.go.

Per-call site naming:
- notify-generic — internal/notification/sender.go (single client across all channel types in the package)
- notify-discord, notify-slack, notify-webhook — internal/api/notification_handler.go (per-channel test endpoints; non-discord/slack senders fall through to notify-webhook)
- github-releases — system_handler.go GitHub releases lookup
- system-dns-check — system_handler.go workers /healthz probe (name as per prompt)
- devtools-tile-probe — devtools_handler.go Tesla Fleet API HEAD probe (name as per prompt)
- tesla-auth — internal/tesla/auth.go OAuth token requests
- geocoder-nominatim, geocoder-google, geocoder-azure, geocoder-search — geocoding package
- eia — gasprices.NewEIAAdapter default client (overridable via WithHTTPClient for tests)

Worker isolation: notification-worker and automation-worker each construct their own asyncAPICallLogger against api_call_log_repo and drain it on graceful shutdown. They never share the API server's logger because they run as separate processes. Both call notification.SetSink with the local sink before MQTT consumers start; automation worker also calls tesla.SetAuthSink so token refreshes from background automations are captured.

=== CHANGES ===
internal/notification/sender.go: replaced package-level bare httpClient with httputil.NewClient(Name='notify-generic') under sync.RWMutex; SetSink(sink) rebuilds with sink installed; senderClient() helper used by sendWebhook/sendNtfy/postJSON.
internal/api/system_handler.go: added apiOutboundSinkMu+apiOutboundSink registry, exported SetOutboundSink(sink), unexported currentOutboundSink() reader. Inlined httputil.NewClient at GitHub releases call (Name='github-releases') and workers /healthz probe (Name='system-dns-check', name per prompt despite probe semantics).
internal/api/notification_handler.go: added notifyOutboundClient(name) helper that builds httputil.NewClient(Name=name, Sink=currentOutboundSink()); refactored postJSON(clientName, url, payload); Discord->'notify-discord', Slack->'notify-slack', Telegram/Pushover/Webhook/Ntfy->'notify-webhook'.
internal/api/devtools_handler.go: tile probe now built via httputil.NewClient(Name='devtools-tile-probe', Sink=currentOutboundSink()) per request.
internal/tesla/auth.go: introduced package-level authHTTPClient (default Name='tesla-auth', no sink) + SetAuthSink(sink, timeout) setter + authClient() reader. tokenRequest now dispatches via authClient().Do(req) so OAuth code/refresh exchanges land in api_call_logs with service='tesla-auth' distinctly from Fleet API rows. Fleet client.go untouched (its SetLogCallback path remains the single source of service='tesla-api').
internal/geocoding/nominatim.go: introduced package-level geoOutboundSink registry + SetSink(sink) setter + currentGeoSink() reader; NewClient now constructs httputil.NewClient(Name='geocoder-nominatim', Sink=currentGeoSink()).
internal/geocoding/google.go: NewGoogleClient -> httputil.NewClient(Name='geocoder-google', Sink=currentGeoSink()).
internal/geocoding/azure.go: NewAzureClient -> httputil.NewClient(Name='geocoder-azure', Sink=currentGeoSink()).
internal/geocoding/search.go: NewSearcher -> httputil.NewClient(Name='geocoder-search', Sink=currentGeoSink()).
internal/adapter/gasprices/eia.go: default constructor httpClient now built via httputil.NewClient(Name='eia', EnableLogging=true); WithHTTPClient(c *http.Client) option preserved for tests.
internal/adapter/tesla/client.go: NOT migrated. Verified zero production importers via 'grep -r "internal/adapter/tesla\"" cmd/ internal/' (no matches). Per prompt: 'only migrate if it is wired into production paths; otherwise leave as-is and document why in the log.'
cmd/teslasync/main.go: after building outboundAPILogSink at line 239, calls api.SetOutboundSink, notification.SetSink, geocoding.SetSink, tesla.SetAuthSink BEFORE the first geocoding.NewGeocoder/EIA/notify call. EIA adapter constructed with gasprices.WithHTTPClient(httputil.NewClient(...Sink: outboundAPILogSink)).
cmd/notification-worker/main.go: builds its own APICallLogger (only when cfg.APILogs.Enabled) + APICallSinkAdapter, calls notification.SetSink(sink) before MQTT consumer start. On graceful shutdown drains via context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second) — fresh ctx, NOT the cancelled root ctx (avoids dropping queued rows).
cmd/automation-worker/main.go: same pattern as notification-worker, additionally calls tesla.SetAuthSink(sink, cfg.Tesla.Timeout) because the automation worker's tesla.NewClient may trigger OAuth refresh exchanges via auth.tokenRequest.

